INT. APARTMENT BUILDING - STAIRWELL - NIGHT

Concrete steps. A buzzing bulb on a timer. Graffiti on the rail.

NADIA (30s, grocery bags, headphones) climbs, humming. She pauses on the fourth-floor landing. The bulb clicks off. Dark.

She fumbles for the switch. Finds it. Click. Light.

Standing three steps above her: ISAAC (40s, her neighbor, bathrobe, bare feet). He is perfectly still. He stares straight ahead.

NADIA
Isaac? You scared me.

He says nothing. She lowers her bags.

NADIA (CONT'D)
Isaac, are you okay?

He turns his head. Slowly. His eyes are blank, rolled back.

She steps down. He steps down. She backs against the rail. He keeps coming, his lips moving.

ISAAC
(a whisper)
Don't turn the light off.

NADIA
What?

The bulb buzzes. Clicks. Dark. A wet breath in her ear.

The light snaps on. MR. OKORO (70s, building super, toolbelt, flashlight) stands on the landing below, thumb on the switch.

MR. OKORO
Nadia! Why are you two standing in the dark?

Isaac blinks. Sways. Looks around, bewildered, as if waking.

ISAAC
Sleepwalking again. I'm sorry.

He climbs back up the stairs, slow and sheepish. Nadia exhales, shaking.

MR. OKORO
You okay?

NADIA
Fine.

She grabs her bags and, without turning around, takes the stairs two at a time.
